PROBLEM STATEMENT: DESIGN STACK OVERFLOW (LOW-LEVEL DESIGN)

Design an in-memory Object-Oriented system for a Q&A platform like Stack Overflow.
The system should allow users to post questions, submit answers, add comments,
vote on posts, and gain reputation points.


1. FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
User Management:
  * Users can create profiles and hold a reputation score.
  * System should support roles (e.g., Guest, Member, Moderator).

Content Creation:
  * A user can post a Question with a title, body, and 1 to 5 Tags.
  * A user can post an Answer to a specific Question.
  * A user can add a Comment to a Question or an Answer.

Voting & Acceptance:
  * Users can Upvote or Downvote Questions and Answers.
  * Users can Upvote Comments.
  * The question author can select exactly one Answer as "Accepted".
  * Users cannot vote on their own posts, nor vote twice on the same post.

Reputation & Badges:
  * Question Upvoted: +10 points to question author.
  * Answer Upvoted: +10 points to answer author.
  * Answer Accepted: +15 points to answer author, +2 points to question author.
  * Question/Answer Downvoted: -2 points to post author.

Search & Filtering:
  * Users can search questions by Keyword, Tag, or Author.
  * Questions can be sorted by Recent, Top Voted, or Unanswered.

Notifications:
  * Notify question authors when an answer or comment is added.
  * Notify answer authors when their answer is accepted or commented on.